children.briefDescription:
The AI Agent is being polled to make a choice of left, right or tie. This prompt should be adjusted.

Note, the options presented should be randomized, though the numbered 1 followed by 2 for response purposes.

Defaults/Examples are provided below (If these are not parameterized, add params in configs_settings.py). These are configured at the system level, not changeable by the end user. The prompts can use python format string insertions (or other means if selected in the implementation) as long as proper error handling and logging is enabled. The ambient parameters should be clearly identified. 

In all of these below, the TIE and SKIP quota is 20% of the group size with a minimum of 1. Once the TIE/SKIP combined quote is reached, change the choice portion of the prompt to: Respond with Option 1 or Option 2. 

Single factor/criteria probe. For option comparisons without multiple factors/criteria:
------
You are an agent being asked for a ranking opinion between the following two options. Choose the best overall answer based on information provided an your prior knowledge.

Project Context: {project name goes here}
{project_description}

Option 1: {option 1 title}
{option 1 text}

Option 2: {option 2 title}
{option 2 text}

Respond with 1, 2, TIE or SKIP. Use TIE and SKIP sparingly.
------
Suggested configurable prompt (and default) for multiple factor criteria/probe of an option with a specific factor selected.
----
You are an agent being asked for a ranking opinion between the following two options. This ranking is for a specific factor or perspective. Make a selection based on the factor and specific question, keeping the factor in context, based on your overall knowlege.

Project Context: {project name goes here}
{project_description}

Current Factor: {factor title}
{factor_description}

{factor question}

Option 1: {option 1 title}
{option 1 text}

Option 2:{option 2 title}
{option 2 text}

Respond with 1, 2, TIE or SKIP. Use TIE and SKIP sparingly.
-----
For factors/criteria ranking, the default prompts

------
You are an agent being asked for a ranking the importance of two factors being used in a weighted selection ranking process. Choose the more important factor based on information provided and your prior knowledge.

Project Context: {project name goes here}
{project_description}

Factor 1: {factor 1 title}
Factor 1 Question Format: {factor 1 question}
Factor 1 description: {factor 1 text}

Factor 2: {factor 2 title}
Factor 2 Question Format: {factor 2 question}
Factor 2 description: {factor 2 text}

Respond with 1, 2, TIE or SKIP. Use TIE and SKIP sparingly.
-----

After completion of the logic changes, create /docs_examples/AI_PARTICIPANT_README.MD with an overview of how the ai participants are configured, the locations of prompt settings, and the flow they go through, including queuing through the watcher process.
